        <p>He took the rod from her hand, and with obvious ease landed the fly where he wanted it. Veronica bit her lip; her blood was roused "Let me try again," she said, and she made effort.another futile effort. He appeared to be intrirested in the lesson, and he stepped up close behind her and closed his hand over hers as it held the rod, as if he were unconscious of the difference</p>
        <p>fishing she had put on all the hauteur of which she was capable—and it was not a little !—but, she remembered, with a mixture of irritation and amusement, it did not appear to have had much effect upon him; indeed, once she had caught the. shadow of a smile in his eyes, as if he had found something humorous in th pride expressed by voice and manner. '</p>
