        <p>Let your correspondent seriously study the true history of trades unionism, and he will not then have the effrontery -to again write such arrant nonsense on this subject. The political success achieved by conscientious trustworthy Labour stalwarts like Burt, Burns, Broad- hurst, and Fenwick, in addition to the effective work already done by Bell, Maddison, Vivian, and John Ward, conclusively prove the needlessness of this new fangled policy proposed by your well-meaning, but apparently inexperienced contiibutor. Mr. Wilson, Secretary of the Sailors' Union, truth- fully stated at a Warrington meeting that he had done more for the sailors than the whole of the I.L.Peers put together:. _ . .</p>
        <p>WilFSocialist Trades Unionists please take note? —louts etc.,</p>
