        <p>GOLF. MERSEY v. HOUGH GREEN.—Played on Saturday at Penketh. The home team won by five matches to two. Scores : MERSEi. HOUGH GREEN'. F. W. Gilbert 1 F. Brown 0 E. G. Medley 1 R. Craig T. Miniati %V. S. Knowles IL N. Foster A. W. Paul Dr. Lindsay 0 C. It. Lewis 0 H. Unswqrti: E. Hartland 0 A. .1. Wilkinson Total 5 To tal THE QUEEN AND. MESSRS. TUCK'S POSTCARDS. Owing to the Qoeen's departure from London and the consequent great press of engagements during the few remaining days, Her Majesty was unable to visit Messrs. Raphael Tuck and Sons' Exhibition of " Post- card Home Decorations," Postcard Tours, and Postcard originals at the Royal Institute of Painters in Water Colours, Piccadilly, and commanded a number of the leading exhibits to be sent to Buckingham Palace.where a miniature Exhibition of all three sections of their Royal Institute Exhibition was arranged by Mr. Adolph Tuck, the Managing Director, for inspection by Her Majesty. The Queen was greatly interested in the remarkable adaptability of artistic Postcards as shown in the Exhibits of both the "Home Decorations," and "Tours," and made a number of purchases of the work of competitors in both sect iofs of the Exhibition, and of the Postcard Originals shown by Messrs. Tuck. The Exhibition will continue at the Royal Institute till AngustlOth,and Messrs. Raphael Tuck have decided to devote the proceeds from Admissions and Catalogues for the remaining period to the Lord Mayor's Crippled Children's Fund.</p>
