        <p>Births. BERRY.—On July 28, at Parklands, Bowdon, Cheshire, to Mr. and Mrs. Berry, a daughter. BUTL.—On the 29th July at -I, \Vhitby-road, Fallowfield, the wife of T. W. Butt, jun. of a son. GERRA RD.—On July 29, at 45,Cavendish-road,Chorlton- cum-Hardy, to Mr. and Mrs. Harry Gerrard, a daughter. FIE AP. —On the 23th July at 65, Palatine-road, Withing- ton, Manchester, the wife of Arthur C. Heap of a daughter. POTTER.—At the Manse, Monton, Eccles, on the 28th July to Rev. G. W and Mrs. Potter, a daughter. Marriages. G COG EON —FITZSINIO.N.S. —On the 29th July at St. Vincent's Church, Altrincham, Cheshire, William Christopher Gudgeon, eldest son of Robert Gudgeon, Netherby, Ayr, to Dorothy Monica' eldest daughter of Frederic John Fitzsimons, High Bank, Altrincham, Cheshire. At home, 4, Melrose Avenue, Rutherglen, Glasgow, 4th and 6th October. MASON—E DWA RDS.—On the 27th July at St. Paul's Church, Withington, by the Rev. W. Muzzle, rector Ernest Edwin Mason, of Levenshulme, to Elizabeth A. Gwendolen, youngest daughter of Councillor S. Edwards, M.A. of Withington. At home, 8, Circular' road, Withington, September 18 and 19. RANDLES ARDSON.—JuIy 28th, at the Parish Church, Warrington, by the Rev. Canon 'Willis,George Heacock Randles to Sarah Richardson. EAVE—KNF.E.—JuIy 29th, at the Parish Church, Warrington by the Rev. Canon Willis, John Gleave to Lizzie Knee. Deaths. BENNETT—JuIy 27th, 1907, at Calla House, Garstallgt 1 William Grange, eldEst son of Mr. John Bennett, Grange Mount, Padgate, aged 47 years. Friends please accept this, the only, intimation.</p>
